# Day 22

## Experiment Title

Creating a Multi Container Application using Docker Compose


## Objective

To understand how Docker Compose can be used to create and manage multiple containers together in a single application environment.


## Theory

Docker Compose allows users to run multiple containers simultaneously by defining services inside a docker-compose.yml file. Each service represents a separate container such as a web server, database, or backend application.

Docker Compose automatically creates a network between containers so that services can communicate with each other easily. It simplifies the deployment and management of multi container applications.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and ensure that Docker services are running properly.

Create a docker-compose.yml file containing multiple services.

Configure the required images and ports for each service.

Start the multi container application using Docker Compose.

Verify that all containers are running successfully.

Observe the communication between the containers through Docker networking.


## Output

Multiple containers were successfully created and executed using Docker Compose.

NGINX and Redis containers were running together inside the same application environment.

Docker Compose automatically managed the networking between both containers.


## Result

Successfully created and managed a multi container application using Docker Compose.
